---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  locale="en"
  route="quiz"
  canonicalPath="/en/privacy/"
  alternatePath="/pt-br/privacidade/"
  indexable={false}
  showGameNavigation={false}
  pageMeta={{
    title: "Privacy and analytics",
    description: "How K-pop Quiz uses visit analytics, cookies and consent choices.",
  }}
>
  <article id="privacy-notice" class="privacy-notice">
    <p class="kicker">K-pop Quiz</p>
    <h1>Privacy and analytics</h1>
    <p>Updated September 24, 2026.</p>

    <h2>Controller and contact</h2>
    <p>K-pop Quiz determines how this site configures analytics. For privacy questions or requests, email <a href="mailto:email@pedrosatin.com">email@pedrosatin.com</a>.</p>

    <h2>Browsing data</h2>
    <p>Cloudflare processes technical request data to deliver the site and reduce abuse. This data may include IP address, traffic routing, system configuration, and traffic information. Cloudflare handles this data under its <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/policies/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.</p>
    <p>Cloudflare Web Analytics measures visited pages and performance. Cloudflare states that the tool does not use its own cookies or collect personal data. This measurement remains active regardless of the choice about Google Analytics.</p>

    <h2>Google Analytics</h2>
    <p>Google Analytics 4 loads only after you agree. It uses cookies and identifiers to measure use of the site and produce audience statistics. Google processes this data under its <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">privacy policy</a>.</p>

    <h2>Analytics choices</h2>
    <p>The banner lets you accept or reject Google Analytics cookies and identifiers. Cloudflare Web Analytics continues measuring site usage. The banner disappears after your choice. Use the "Privacy preferences" button in the footer to change your choice. Rejecting Google Analytics stops new GA4 measurement on this and later visits.</p>

    <h2>Sharing and retention</h2>
    <p>Cloudflare metrics are available in the Cloudflare dashboard. Accepted GA4 metrics are available in the site’s Google Analytics property for the retention period configured there. The site does not sell browsing data.</p>

    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>You can ask about data processing, correct data, request deletion where applicable, or revoke GA4 consent. Use the email above.</p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
